{"paper": "SSC-DelhiPoliceConstable-21-Nov-2023-Shift3.pdf", "status": "ok", "mode": "sequential", "splitter": "qdot", "section_slice": true, "extracted_count": 15, "tagged_count": 15, "questions": [{"n": 1, "text": "Which ratio is the greatest among the following?", "options": [{"text": "5 : 8", "added": false}, {"text": "4 : 7", "added": false}, {"text": "3 : 5", "added": false}, {"text": "1 : 3", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "ratio-basics", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 2, "text": "A sum of ₹2,400 yields a simple interest of ₹460 in 2 years and 4 months. The rate of interest per annum is:", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simple Interest", "sub": "si-formula", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 3, "text": "Anjali and Manju together can do a piece of work in 5 days. If Anjali does twice as much work as Manju in a given time, how long would Anjali alone take to do the work?", "options": [{"text": "6 days", "added": false}, {"text": "7.5 days", "added": false}, {"text": "7 days", "added": false}, {"text": "6.5 days", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Work", "sub": "efficiency", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 4, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Profit-Loss", "sub": "profit-loss-percent", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 5, "text": "The price of a car increased by 25%. By what percentage should the price now be reduced to bring it to the actual price?", "options": [{"text": "20%", "added": false}, {"text": "25%", "added": false}, {"text": "15%", "added": false}, {"text": "35%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "increase-decrease", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 6, "text": "A train covers a distance of 10 km in 10 minutes. If its speed is decreased by 20 km/h, then the time taken by it to cover the same distance will be:",